(
  schema_version: 1,
  id: "m5_chassis_wreck_eject",
  display_name: "M5 Chassis Wreck & Eject",
  description: "M5 acceptance proof per spec/native-implementation-backlog M5-001..M5-004 + roadmap done-criteria. Player is a Powered Armor pilot facing one Light Mech adversary. The mech's heavy autocannon will wreck the player's chassis through layered armor (External → Internal → Core → wound) emitting `chassis.armor_layer_damaged` / `armor_zone_destroyed` / `module_state_changed` / `stage_changed` events along the way. WIN path: pilot ejects before the chassis hits Wreck stage, runs to the extraction zone as foot infantry — emits `chassis.pilot_ejected` + `pilot_separated` + `mission.mission_resolved {result: won}`. LOSS path: pilot waits too long → `chassis.pilot_bailed_too_late` + `mission.mission_resolved {result: lost, reason: player_dead}`. Reuses M1.5 cf-mission + cf-ai unchanged.",
  seed: 53,
  duration_ticks: Some(7200),
